 "library": {
  "title": "Air source heat pump 7 kW monobloc, see-through cutaway",
  "description": "Domestic air-to-water monobloc heat pump (7 kW, R32) at real size, 1100 x 450 x 765 mm casing on rubber feet and a concrete pad, built to show the inside. Front, top, right and back shields and the partition are see-through glass; the casing frame stays opaque. Fan side: swept 3-blade fan with DC motor on struts, bellmouth shroud and ringed grille, L-shaped evaporator coil (aluminium fins with a cut-away window, two staggered rows of copper tubes, return bends, distributor capillaries, suction header). Compressor side: rotary compressor with heater band, grommets and terminal box, accumulator, 4-way reversing valve with pilot solenoid, electronic expansion valve, filter drier, pressure switches, Schrader ports, brazed plate heat exchanger with chevron plates. Refrigerant pipes are routed square with bends and colour-coded (hot gas red, liquid orange, suction blue with insulation). Water side: circulating pump, flow switch, air vent, safety valve, pressure gauge reading 0-4 bar, 8 L expansion vessel teed into the return, isolation valves with red/blue levers, lagged flow/return pipes dropping into a duct. Control box with inverter PCB, capacitors, relays, heatsink and cables to every component. 19 named sub-Objects inside one Object, generated from an OpenSCAD program.",
